Subject: [PATCH] esp32/p4: no esp_cam_sensor sensor driver built in for any P4 variant

cameraif knows its cameras as descriptions frozen into the image, so none of
Espressif's per-sensor drivers is compiled: each is a few KB to 30 KB of
flash that the description of the same sensor costs less of. The fragment this
adds is the place to turn a driver on again (CONFIG_CAMERA_<chip> and its
AUTO_DETECT_MIPI_INTERFACE_SENSOR), and cameraif's own micropython.cmake says
why both are needed.

A fragment on the P4 common config rather than on one variant, because the
CSI controller is a property of the chip, not of which radio is attached.

diff --git a/ports/esp32/boards/mpconfigboard_esp32p4_common.cmake b/ports/esp32/boards/mpconfigboard_esp32p4_common.cmake
index 876a186de..d61916f2a 100644
--- a/ports/esp32/boards/mpconfigboard_esp32p4_common.cmake
+++ b/ports/esp32/boards/mpconfigboard_esp32p4_common.cmake
@@ -3,4 +3,5 @@ set(IDF_TARGET esp32p4)
 set(SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS
     boards/sdkconfig.base
     boards/sdkconfig.p4
+    boards/sdkconfig.p4_camera
 )
diff --git a/ports/esp32/boards/sdkconfig.p4_camera b/ports/esp32/boards/sdkconfig.p4_camera
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..6c2e8bd74
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ports/esp32/boards/sdkconfig.p4_camera
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# cameraif on the ESP32-P4: no esp_cam_sensor sensor driver is built in.
+#
+# Every camera cameraif knows is a description in sensors/, frozen into every P4
+# image and tried by Camera() in turn (cameraif_sensors.NAMES): the board names
+# the pins, never the sensor, and a camera with no description is a Python file
+# passed as sensor=, not a firmware build. The descriptions are smaller than the
+# drivers they replace.
+#
+# Building one of Espressif's drivers in anyway takes two options each: without
+# CONFIG_CAMERA_<chip> the driver is not compiled; without its
+# AUTO_DETECT_MIPI_INTERFACE_SENSOR option esp_cam_sensor does not emit the
+# `-u` that keeps its probe against --gc-sections. Camera() walks those probes
+# before the descriptions.
+#
+# patches/0002 carries the same (empty) settings for a MicroPython tree outside
+# build_mp.py; tests/check_sensor_configs.py checks that the two agree and that
+# every driver in the pinned esp_cam_sensor is described or named as one that
+# can't be.
